    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d778">

                <pb facs="0739" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/49: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-11T18:00:00+01:20">September 11,
                            1939—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 12—7:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>169. For the Secretary and Under Secretary. My 167, September 10, 1 p.m.<anchor
                        n="15" xml:id="d778-f1"/> Dutch and Belgians have agreed on identic note.
                    Conditionally being put before the Oslo States with the suggestion that if they
                    wish they can send a similar note but they are being told that whether they do
                    or not the Dutch and Belgians will send this note in reply to the British
                    proposal. As soon as note is delivered to British I will be given a copy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gordon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d778-f1" n="15" xml:id="d778-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported a meeting of the Belgian and Netherland Foreign
                    Ministers at Breda, September 11, in an endeavor to reach agreement on an
                    identic reply to the British proposal (740.00112 European War 1939/40).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
